From 5eb3b06d3c2e30069f6fc05ae7d85f1af1f3a432 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 4.8" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1158 redfin: qmux retry pre-registration BindMuxDataPort
 (kern.sweet_wds_bindfix, default on)

On a cold boot the SIM PIN is entered late. CommCenter sets up its WDS data
clients once at launch while the SIM is still PIN-locked/unregistered and binds
a data port (WDS BindMuxDataPort 0x00a2); the modem rejects the bind (error 0x3,
not registered). CommCenter treats the bind as done and never re-binds, so the
cid stays unbound -> defaults to mux 0, and every later StartNetworkInterface
targets the dead mux 0 and fails forever. Restarting CommCenter fixes it only
because the re-bind then happens after registration.

With kern.sweet_wds_bindfix = 1 (default), the router intercepts the modem's
rejection of a BindMuxDataPort (d_answer): it flips the result TLV 0x02 to
success {0,0} in place so CommCenter records cid->mux (and we set our own
cid->mux to match), and records the bind as pending-retry. data_poll re-issues
the bind to the modem on CommCenter's own WDS client port (d_own_send, so the
modem's answer is caught by the router and not forwarded to CommCenter) every
~1.5 s until the registered modem accepts it. The matching StartNetworkInterface
is held (d_cid_ready) until the bind is confirmed, so it is never serviced
against mux 0. kern.sweet_wds_bindfix = 0 restores k26 exactly (modem error
forwarded as-is, no retry, no gating). The immediate-success bind path is
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvABzcjCeDywTuc6ppYmC
